from pathlib import Path
import json,html,csv,hashlib,zipfile
B=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
r=json.loads((B/'output/results.json').read_text())
records={}
for policy in r['nominal']:
    with (B/f'output/{policy}.csv').open() as f:
        rows=list(csv.reader(f)); records[policy]=[[float(x) for x in row] for row in rows[1::5]]
summary=''.join('<tr><td>'+policy+'</td>'+''.join(f'<td>{v[k]:.3f}</td>' for k in ['final_burden','min_reserve','final_resistant_fraction','input_integral'])+'</tr>' for policy,v in r['nominal'].items())
page='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Virtual Body — Cancer Research Prototype</title><style>body{font:17px/1.65 system-ui;background:#101b28;color:#ecf1f5;margin:0}main{max-width:1050px;margin:auto;padding:28px}h1{font-size:clamp(30px,5vw,52px);line-height:1.2}a{color:#7dd9e8}button,select,input{font:inherit}button,select{background:#263e50;color:white;border:1px solid #81a7b9;padding:8px;border-radius:5px}.controls{display:flex;gap:15px;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center}.panel{padding:20px;background:#1b2e40;border-radius:12px;margin:25px 0}img{max-width:100%;background:white}svg{width:100%;height:auto}table{border-collapse:collapse;font-size:15px;width:100%}td,th{padding:10px;text-align:left;border-bottom:1px solid #547083}.scroll{overflow-x:auto}.dim{color:#bdced9}summary{cursor:pointer}:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #f6c66b;outline-offset:4px}</style></head><body><main><p class="dim">Michael Emanuel Glover · Developed with Codex · 4 October 2026</p><h1>The virtual body:<br>cells, niches, organs, organism</h1><p>An executable starting point for studying malignant populations alongside resistant clones, immune activity, resource supply, exposure and healthy-tissue preservation.</p><div class="panel"><strong>Synthetic, dimensionless and uncalibrated.</strong> These are engineering experiments with invented parameter values. They do not predict a patient's outcome or establish a cure. The sites below represent aggregate populations, not resolved individual cells.</div><p><a href="RESEARCH-PLAN.md">Research plan and equations</a> · <a href="output/results.json">All results</a> · <a href="output/verification.json">Numerical checks</a> · <a href="VIRTUAL-BODY-SOURCE.zip">Source bundle</a></p><h2>Inspect the coupled sites</h2><div class="controls"><label>Fictional control <select id="policy"><option>none</option><option>continuous</option><option>pulsed</option><option>feedback</option></select></label><button id="play">Play slowly</button><label>Time <input id="time" type="range" min="0" max="200" value="0"></label><output id="stamp"></output></div><svg viewBox="0 0 960 390" role="img" aria-label="Three connected abstract tissue sites with sensitive and resistant populations, resources and healthy reserve"><path d="M180 110H780" stroke="#7799ae" stroke-width="3"/><text x="480" y="30" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ecf1f5">Systemic exposure connects three abstract sites</text><g id="sites"></g></svg><p id="status" aria-live="polite"></p><p class="dim">Cyan: sensitive population. Orange: resistant population. Circle area scales with population. Reserve, resource and immune activity appear below each site. Slider frames are sampled from the executed simulation; no new simulation runs in this page.</p><h2>Nominal outcomes at dimensionless time 50</h2><div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Control</th><th>Final burden</th><th>Minimum reserve</th><th>Resistant fraction</th><th>Integrated input</th></tr></thead><tbody>SUMMARY</tbody></table></div><p>The continuous-control run suppresses sensitive populations while resistance dominates the residual tumor and healthy reserve declines. Feedback retains more reserve in this assumed model but leaves greater final burden. This comparison does not identify a clinical optimum.</p><img src="output/trajectories.png" alt="Executed tumor, resistant population, reserve and exposure trajectories for four synthetic controls."><h2>Parameter sensitivity</h2><p>Twenty-four shared parameter draws per control expose how arbitrary assumptions change the result. These points are not patients or confidence intervals.</p><img src="output/tradeoffs.png" alt="Synthetic parameter sensitivity scatter comparing tumor burden with reserve."><h2>Where your HRL algorithm enters</h2><p>The unchanged sparse HRL engine labels a separate 120-cell synthetic patch benchmark. Accuracy: priors alone 55.8%; pairwise factors 68.3%; pairwise plus three-way factors 70.0%. All three converged. A separate unknown-label demonstration rejected 12 cells. Compatibility is correct by construction in this toy dataset; these results are not biological validation or calibrated confidence.</p><p>The inference and dynamical components remain separate. A measured observation model, cell-state-to-rate mapping and external validation are required to connect them responsibly.</p><h2>The next experiment</h2><p>Select one cancer context, version one perturbation dataset, fit only identifiable parameters, and test response predictions on held-out donors and interventions. Compare HRL with simpler baselines before increasing model complexity.</p><p><a href="https://www.cancer.gov/about-nci/organization/dcb/research-programs/csbc">NCI cancer systems biology</a> · <a href="https://docs.humantumoratlas.org/data_access/introduction/">Human Tumor Atlas data</a> · <a href="https://depmap.org/portal/data_page/">DepMap datasets</a> · <a href="https://physicell.org/">PhysiCell</a></p></main><script>const data=DATA;const slider=document.getElementById('time'),policy=document.getElementById('policy'),play=document.getElementById('play');let timer=null;function render(){const rows=data[policy.value];slider.max=rows.length-1;const row=rows[Math.min(+slider.value,rows.length-1)];document.getElementById('stamp').textContent=row[0].toFixed(2);let svg='';for(let i=0;i<3;i++){const x=180+i*300,b=2+i*5,s=row[b],r=row[b+1];svg+=`<text x="${x}" y="65" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ecf1f5">Site ${i+1}</text><circle cx="${x-48}" cy="150" r="${65*Math.sqrt(s)}" fill="#56d3dd"/><circle cx="${x+48}" cy="150" r="${65*Math.sqrt(r)}" fill="#f6a553"/><text x="${x}" y="250" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ecf1f5">S ${s.toFixed(3)} · R ${r.toFixed(3)}</text><text x="${x}" y="280" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ecf1f5">Reserve ${row[b+4].toFixed(3)}</text><text x="${x}" y="310" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ecf1f5">Resource ${row[b+3].toFixed(3)}</text><text x="${x}" y="340" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ecf1f5">Immune ${row[b+2].toFixed(3)}</text>`;}document.getElementById('sites').innerHTML=svg;document.getElementById('status').textContent=`Input ${row[1].toFixed(2)} · systemic exposure ${row[17].toFixed(3)} · dimensionless synthetic values`;}function stop(){clearInterval(timer);timer=null;play.textContent='Play slowly';}play.onclick=()=>{if(timer){stop();return;}if(+slider.value>=+slider.max)slider.value=0;timer=setInterval(()=>{slider.value=+slider.value+1;render();if(+slider.value>=+slider.max)stop();},250);play.textContent='Pause';};slider.oninput=()=>{stop();render();};policy.onchange=()=>{stop();render();};render();</script></body></html>'''
addition="""<h2>Drive audit: measured data and new calculations</h2><p>The expanded accessible-storage inventory covered 880,934 files; 45,884 selected text/code files were searched. It located the existing HRL2026 virtual-cell code and a cached dataset of 5,310 measured CRISPR assay ranks. Coverage and exclusions are recorded in the <a href="AUDIT-RESULTS.md">full audit report</a>; private raw inventory and physiology records are excluded from this publication.</p><p>New sequence-disjoint and gene-disjoint evaluations use existing sequence features and sparse HRL. The original row-based split shared 271 distinct test sequences with training. All ten new HRL fits converged; their small point-estimate gains do not establish significant superiority.</p><img src="output/crispr-benchmark.png" alt="Measured assay-rank benchmark comparing one-hot Ridge, existing sequence features and the HRL graph extension."><p><a href="output/crispr-benchmark.json">Benchmark results and provenance</a></p><p>An isolated virtual-cell snapshot fixes the original missing-method crash, entropy normalization, state-change reporting and abstention coding. A seven-node, three-level hierarchy passed ten recursive steps. These remain categorical computations, not physical human-cell simulations. <a href="output/nested-cell-checks.json">See execution checks</a>.</p><h2>Can this synthetic model sustain tumor-free stability?</h2><p>A new eigenvalue analysis finds that the nominal resistant-population stability threshold requires constant dimensionless exposure above 5.181195, while maintaining the assumed reserve floor of 0.7 allows at most 0.136364. The feasible intersection is empty at the nominal settings and in all 24 arbitrary parameter configurations.</p><img src="output/extinction-feasibility.png" alt="Synthetic model invasion eigenvalues and equilibrium healthy reserve versus constant exposure; their required intervals do not overlap."><p>This is a local-stability result for constant exposure in the implemented model. It does not establish the behavior of arbitrary schedules, actual cancer biology or patients. <a href="output/extinction-feasibility.json">Full stability calculations</a>.</p>"""
page=page.replace('<h2>The next experiment</h2>',addition+'<h2>Validation still needed</h2>')
(B/'report.html').write_text(page.replace('SUMMARY',summary).replace('DATA',json.dumps(records,separators=(',',':'))))
src=Path('/home/rmichaelglover/Code/relaxation-labeling/python/hrl_generic/engine.py')
if src.exists():
 assert src.read_bytes()==(B/'vendor/hrl_engine.py').read_bytes()
else:
 assert hashlib.sha256((B/'vendor/hrl_engine.py').read_bytes()).hexdigest()==json.loads((B/'provenance.json').read_text())['sha256']
if src.exists():
 (B/'provenance.json').write_text(json.dumps({'source_path':str(src),'sha256':hashlib.sha256(src.read_bytes()).hexdigest(),'copied_without_modification':True,'clinical_data_used':False,'date':'2026-10-04'},indent=2))
files=[p for p in sorted(B.rglob('*')) if p.is_file() and '__pycache__' not in str(p) and 'audit' not in p.relative_to(B).parts and p.name not in ['manifest.json','VIRTUAL-BODY-SOURCE.zip']]
(B/'manifest.json').write_text(json.dumps({'files':[{'path':str(p.relative_to(B)),'sha256':hashlib.sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest()} for p in files]},indent=2))
with zipfile.ZipFile(B/'VIRTUAL-BODY-SOURCE.zip','w',zipfile.ZIP_DEFLATED) as z:
 for p in files+[B/'manifest.json']: z.write(p,Path(B.name)/p.relative_to(B))
print('Report and source archive built')
